From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] session: a refused shutdown must not tear the shell down

shutdown_completed() ran the privileged PowerOff/Reboot call, caught any
DBusException, logged it, and then reached

    # Always quit the shell model to ensure we exit
    self._shell_model.quit()

regardless of whether the system had accepted the request. On a machine where
polkit refuses a non-interactive PowerOff - which is every Aspartame guest -
choosing Shutdown logged
`InteractiveAuthorizationRequired` and then destroyed the desktop while
shutting nothing down, leaving the user at a black screen.

The privileged request now lives in _request_system_shutdown(), which reports
whether the system accepted it. shutdown_completed() only quits on success,
or when the mode is logout, where quitting is the action. A refusal leaves the
session running, clears the pending mode and tells the user through the
existing alert surface.

A refusal is also logged as a plain warning rather than logging.exception(),
so an ordinary denied request no longer looks like a fatal traceback in the
session log or to sugar-gtk4-runtime-check.sh.

